// The tables of the decimal engine: powers of ten, the reciprocals that divide by them, and the DPD codec.
//
// floor(x / 10^k) is the high half of x times a magic number, shifted: with t = high(x × magic), the quotient
// is t >> shift, or ((x - t) / 2 + t) >> (shift - 1) when the add flag is set (Granlund and Montgomery). The
// numbers came from RazorForge's D128.rf, where they were generated and checked, and are checked again on
// random and edge values by the script that wrote this file.

